 EDP to Snowflake data ingestion pipeline: summary, system design and interview guide
This is based on the https://colesgroup.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DIAT/pages/528090246/Cloud+BI+Platform+EDP+to+Snowflake+Data+Ingestion+Pipeline+-+HLD.
1. Summary
Goal: Build a secure, config-driven pipeline that copies full or partial datasets from the Enterprise Data Platform (EDP, which stores Delta Lake tables on Azure Databricks) into Snowflake for BI and data discovery.
What it does:
Detects changes (CDC). It compares the latest published version of a Delta table with the previous one and labels each record Insert, Update/Change or Delete. A full extract is the same output with every record marked "I".
Encrypts the files. Client-side encryption (CSE) uses AES-256 envelope encryption, with the master key in Azure Key Vault. Files are never stored unencrypted in the staging area.
Stages the files in an Azure storage account (ADLS Gen2) that Snowflake reads from (the "external stage").
Loads the files with COPY INTO through an encrypted named stage in Snowflake, which decrypts them during the load.
Applies the changes. A dynamically generated MERGE moves changes from Raw Staging into Persisted Staging, which feeds a dimensional Presentation layer.

