2.8 Non-functional checklist for a new client
Performance and cost: measure baselines across file sizes, Spark cluster sizes and Snowflake warehouse sizes. Use a dedicated loading warehouse with auto-suspend.
Replay: keep the last N batches of files, as long as they are still encrypted with the current key.
Key rotation runbook: process or re-key any files left in the stage before rotating. Files encrypted with the old key can't be read after the switch.
Observability: track status per batch in event_log, compare row counts (source vs RAW vs merged), check COPY_HISTORY, and alert on failures.
Security: RBAC per schema, dynamic data masking for personal information (PI), and a private endpoint for the storage account.
Schema drift: fail fast (the default) or evolve automatically through the metadata.

2.9 Which pattern to choose
Pattern
Use when
Trade-off
#1 Scheduled batch, file-based
Default choice: many sources, strict security
Many moving parts, encryption overhead
#2 Snowpipe micro-batch
Data needed within minutes
MERGE still runs as a batch, tables must exist in advance, schema drift isn't handled
#3 External tables
Discovery or exploration with no copy
